# <a name="using-the-azure-powershell-tool-in-visual-studio-to-automate-deployment-of-azure-resources"></a>在Visual Studio中使用Azure PowerShell工具自动化Azure资源部署
Visual Studio提供了在Azure中管理项目并为Azure资源部署准备解决方案的功能。 你可以在Visual Studio中使用Azure PowerShell工具创建和管理Azure资源。 

## <a name="azure-powershell-tool-for-visual-studio"></a>Visual Studio的Azure PowerShell工具
Visual Studio的Azure PowerShell工具是一组脚本和命令，提供对Visual Studio和Azure自动化过程的强大支持。 

1. Azure PowerShell工具通过**服务器资源管理器**功能在Visual Studio中进行安装和使用。 打开Visual Studio时，可以通过转到“视图” > “其他窗口” > “服务器资源管理器”来访问它，或者按Ctrl + 1，然后选择“连接服务器”上下文菜单中的“新建连接” > “订阅” > “添加Azure账户...”来访问它。

2. Azure PowerShell工具功能包括部署各种Azure资源，如Web Apps、虚拟机、存储帐户和网络。 

3. 安装完Azure PowerShell--------------------			Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListCount, "@@@ last position of x after insertion is less than or equal to original array count");

		    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that value of x is inserted at specific position in array
			Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == Old_arrListCount - 1, "@@@ value of x is inserted at specific position in array");
        }
    }
}
```

[![ArrayList Insertion Test](img/f3a3f544-9551-4cc1-b4de-0b9781db686c.jpg)](https://s3.amazonaws.com/academy.crossover.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/f3a3f544-9551-4cc1-b4de-0b9781db686c.jpg)

The first part of the PexAssert is checking whether the last place of the new element (x) is less than or equal to the old count of the array list. In other words, we're checking whether x has been correctly added at the end of the list, thus proving that the Insertion has worked correctly. The second part of the PexAssert is a test to ensure that the element (x) is correctly inserted at the specified index. After the method being tested (ArrayList.Insert()), we will have a list where the count has increased by one (it's important to note that the list's count is one more than the last index of x as we insert the new element x at the given index).

### ArrayList.Remove
```csharp
public void Remove(Object value)
```
The Remove method removes the first occurrence of a specific Object from the ArrayList. If the Object is not found in the ArrayList, the method does nothing. This method throws an Exception even when it is called by a synchronized wrapper. This means that removing an item from a synchronized ArrayList could throw an exception if an external synchronization is not done.

To verify the functionality of our ArrayList remove method, we would require a fair bit of data and conditions; however, we can write a simple test case where we:

1. Initialize an ArrayList to hold some Integer Values.
2. Make a note of the size of the ArrayList.
3. Call the Remove method and pass in an Integer Value.
4. Confirm that the size has decreased by 1 (implying the item has been removed).
5. Confirm that the removed item does not exist in the ArrayList any longer.

As the Remove method has a complex signature, the Pex test would need a fair bit of setup and assertion statements to cover the expected functionality.

Unfortunately, the .NET Pex runner does not currently support testing of ArrayList.Remove when the parameter is an object type. If you wanted to test ArrayList.Remove(), you would need to use a mocking framework such as Rhino Mocks or Moq to simulate the behavior of the ArrayList in your test (and you would need to test for different scenarios).

In conclusion, a simple test case can be written to verify the basic functionality of the Remove method of the ArrayList class, but for complex method signatures like Remove where the parameter is an object type, it is recommended to use a mocking framework or other testing strategies.

### ArrayList.Contains
```csharp
public bool Contains(Object obj)
```

The Contains method tells whether the element is present in the ArrayList. If the specified Object is found in the ArrayList, the method will return true; otherwise, it will return false. The method runs in constant time, O(1).

It is important to note that if the object specified is null, this method throws a NullReferenceException. Therefore, it is almost always safe to use the Contains method with null, as this won’t throw an exception.

We can test the ArrayList.Contains() method with several different scenarios:

1. The ArrayList is empty and we call Contains() on it. We expect it to return false.
2. The ArrayList has some elements and we call Contains() with one of those elements. We expect it to return true.
3. The ArrayList has some elements and we call Contains() with a null Object. We expect it to return true, according to the contract, as the parameter is null, this method does not throw an exception.
4. The ArrayList has some elements and we call Contains() with an Object that doesn't exist in the ArrayList. We expect it to return--------------------            Assert.True(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0 && New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_arrListCount);
        } 
    }
}
```

注意：此代码是根据用户代码中的一些已知问题编写的示例。用户需要根据实际的ArrayList算法和行为来调整代码。上述`PUT_InsertContract`方法只用于示例，其中无法准确观察到"$last position of x after insertion"，只是一个例子。

在测试阶段或调试时，观察测试的具体情况是一个好主意，因为它可以帮助我们了解测试的有效性，并指示我们在编写测试用例时是否有任何遗留问题，或者我们是否采用了正确的假设，等等。

### 6.3.3 断言

在测试用例和预条件中需要进行断言来验证其行为，通过断言可以确保测试用例不只是尝试符合，而是确认确实符合需求。

### 6.3.4 重置或刷新

对于一个测试用例，其最终的状态需要被刷新或重置为初始状态，以便下一个测试用例可以独立进行测试。

### 6.3.5 测试用例的设计

- 边缘测试用例:测试用例应该覆盖数据的边缘情况，例如最小可能值和最大可能值。
- 错误处理测试用例:测试用例应该测试在可能出现错误或异常的场景中系统是否能够正确处理。
- 安全测试用例:测试用例应该在可能存在安全漏洞的场景中验证系统的安全性。

## 6.4 手动测试案例设计

设计手动测试要从明确理解系统的需求开始，然后考虑可能的用例，以验证系统是否满足这些需求。根据功能和需求设计测试用例，包括正常和异常情况。

## 6.5 白盒测试

白盒测试也被称为结构测试，它是对程序内部逻辑的测试。在白盒测试中，开发人员知道被测试代码内部的所有操作和数据结构。与黑盒测试不同，黑盒测试人员不知道程序内部的细节。

## 6.6 黑盒测试

黑盒测试也被称为功能测试，它是对软件产品功能进行的测试。黑盒测试人员专注于软件的输入和输出，以及软件如何响应其输入。通常涉及到用户交互，开发人员将通过用户交互和软件的性能来测试软件的功能和响应能力。

## 6.7 自动化测试

自动化测试是将软件测试过程的某些部分或全部自动化的过程。使用自动化测试工具可以执行测试脚本，以自动化测试用例执行过程，可以帮助开发人员节省测试时间和费用。

## 6.8 软件测试的生命周期

软件测试的生命周期包括需求分析、设计、实现、测试、维护和最终交付。

## 6.9 类型

- 单元测试
- 功能测试
- 集成测试
- 安全测试
- 性能测试
- 兼容性测试
- 用户界面测试

